  <title>Non-Compliance Letters under 505B(d)(1) of the Federal Food, Drug, and Cosmetic Act</title>
  <link>http://www.fda.gov/drugs/guidance-compliance-regulatory-information/non-compliance-letters-under-505bd1-federal-food-drug-and-cosmetic-act</link>
  <description>Section 505B(d)(1) requires FDA to send a PREA Non-Compliance letter to sponsors who have failed to submit their pediatric assessments required under PREA by the final due date, have failed to seek or obtain a deferral or deferral extension.</description>
